# Shared infrastructure. Source of truth for env:pull / env:push.
#
# Rule:  KEY=value  -> non-secret, used as-is, never touches the secrets backend.
#        KEY=       -> secret, pulled from / pushed to the backend.
# The values below are local-dev defaults (non-secret).
#
# Secrets sync is OPT-IN. By default just `cp .env.example .env` and fill the
# empty (secret) values by hand. To use the pluggable sync instead, pick a
# backend with ONE env var (not stored here — it lives in your shell):
#   SECRETS_BACKEND=localstack pnpm env:pull   # dev/demo: the infra LocalStack vault
#   SECRETS_BACKEND=aws        pnpm env:pull   # a real cloud vault (AWS Secrets Manager)
# `localstack` needs nothing else (dummy creds baked in); seed it once per fresh
# `pnpm infra:up` with `SECRETS_BACKEND=localstack pnpm env:push`. See ADR 0001.
# NB: the AWS_* keys further down are for the Bedrock model provider, NOT sync.

# Infra vs application env are split into two files (ADR 0026, #127). This root
# .env owns the APPLICATION runtime surface: app secrets. The dev-deployment
# concern — the container-password secrets (DB_PASSWORD, REDIS_PASSWORD) compose
# provisions — lives in deploy/.env (see deploy/.env.example). with-env loads
# both, so nothing is duplicated.
#
# The infra provisioning inputs (DB_PORT/USER/NAME, DB_VECTOR_NAME, REDIS_PORT,
# OLLAMA_PORT) are config-as-code and DERIVED for compose by
# scripts/resolve-compose-env.ts (ADR 0026, #126) — no rows here, no drift.
# REDIS_URL likewise lives in @acme/redis/config (default redis://localhost:6379);
# @acme/db and @acme/redis keep runtime process.env overrides for the dynamic case
# (testcontainer mapped port, infra-injected prod endpoint).

# --- localstripe (dependency-free dev billing, default) ------------------
# Billing runs against the local `localstripe` infra service by default — no
# Stripe account or network needed. `pnpm infra:up` seeds the products/plans
# + webhook; grant tiers from the admin page (Set Tier). All dummy non-secret
# values. See docs/adr/0004-localstripe-dev-billing.md.
# To use real Stripe instead: run under the `staging` profile (`APP_ENV=staging`)
# and pull the real keys (`pnpm env:pull`).
# Every non-secret Stripe value is config-as-code now (@acme/billing/config, ADR
# 0026): the plan IDs, publishable key and manage-billing URL (client), and the
# localstripe connection + checkout redirect paths (server, stripeConnectionConfig).
# Only the secrets remain here.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_localstripe
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_localstripe

# Provider selection, model ids, region, embedding dimension, the S3
# endpoint/bucket and the ollama host port/pull IDs are config-as-code now
# (@acme/models/config, @acme/ingest/config, ADR 0026) — no longer env; compose
# derives the ollama port + pull list via scripts/resolve-compose-env.ts. Only the
# provider *secrets* remain below.

# Model-provider secrets — Bedrock (via the AWS chain) + OpenRouter API key.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
